      * Routes order messages from a terminal queue to the shipping
      * terminals: an OS/VS COBOL TCAM program.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. MSGROUTE.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-TEXT          PIC X(80).
       01 WS-WAITING       PIC 9(6).
       01 WS-ENABLE-KEY    PIC X(10).
       COMMUNICATION SECTION.
       CD ORDER-IN FOR INITIAL INPUT
           SYMBOLIC QUEUE IS IN-QUEUE
           SYMBOLIC SUB-QUEUE-1 IS IN-SUBQ
           MESSAGE DATE IS IN-DATE
           MESSAGE TIME IS IN-TIME
           SYMBOLIC SOURCE IS IN-TERMINAL
           TEXT LENGTH IS IN-LENGTH
           END KEY IS IN-END
           STATUS KEY IS IN-STATUS
           MESSAGE COUNT IS IN-COUNT.
       CD SHIP-OUT FOR OUTPUT
           DESTINATION COUNT IS OUT-COUNT
           TEXT LENGTH IS OUT-LENGTH
           STATUS KEY IS OUT-STATUS
           DESTINATION TABLE OCCURS 2 TIMES INDEXED BY OUT-IX
           ERROR KEY IS OUT-ERROR
           SYMBOLIC DESTINATION IS OUT-DEST.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-PARA.
           MOVE 'ORDERS' TO IN-QUEUE
           MOVE SPACES TO IN-SUBQ
           ENABLE INPUT ORDER-IN WITH KEY WS-ENABLE-KEY
           ACCEPT ORDER-IN MESSAGE COUNT
           MOVE IN-COUNT TO WS-WAITING
           PERFORM ROUTE-ONE WS-WAITING TIMES
           DISABLE INPUT ORDER-IN WITH KEY WS-ENABLE-KEY
           STOP RUN.
       ROUTE-ONE.
           RECEIVE ORDER-IN MESSAGE INTO WS-TEXT
               NO DATA GO TO ROUTE-EXIT
           END-RECEIVE
           IF IN-STATUS NOT = '00'
               GO TO ROUTE-EXIT
           END-IF
           MOVE 2 TO OUT-COUNT
           MOVE IN-LENGTH TO OUT-LENGTH
           SET OUT-IX TO 1
           MOVE 'SHIP01' TO OUT-DEST (OUT-IX)
           SET OUT-IX TO 2
           MOVE 'SHIP02' TO OUT-DEST (OUT-IX)
           SEND SHIP-OUT FROM WS-TEXT WITH EMI
           IF OUT-STATUS NOT = '00'
               PURGE SHIP-OUT
           END-IF.
       ROUTE-EXIT.
           EXIT.
